 "notes": "Printed p.145. Columns 38-49: Total vernaculars of India foreign to Rajputana, Marathi, Panjabi (includes Western Panjabi), Gujarati. Gujarati Dungarpur persons printed '2 185' (comma missing/broken). Discrepancy: Total foreign vernaculars, Bundi, males is printed 881 as read at high zoom, but 1,452 - 621 = 831; the column sum against RAJPUTANA (80,141) also needs 831; Marathi+Panjabi+Gujarati+Bihari+Eastern Hindi+Others for Bundi males = 831; and Vernaculars of India minus Rajputana (113,081 - 112,250) = 831. So the true figure is 831. Either the middle digit is a 3 so heavily inked that it looks closed, or it is a misprint. It is transcribed as printed (881). Nil cells ('...') are omitted, and a nil persons/males/females cell inside a record is given as null."
